@startuml
title Socket API Flow — One Connection, Successful Calls
state "Server" as server {
  state "socket()" as ss
  state "bind()" as sb
  state "listen()" as sl
  state "accept() -> connected fd" as sa
  state "read()/write() on connected fd" as sr
  state "close(connected fd)" as sc
  [*] --> ss
  ss --> sb
  sb --> sl
  sl --> sa
  sa --> sr
  sr --> sc
  sc --> [*]
}
state "Client" as client {
  state "socket()" as cs
  state "connect()" as cc
  state "read()/write()" as cr
  state "close()" as cx
  [*] --> cs
  cs --> cc
  cc --> cr
  cr --> cx
  cx --> [*]
}
note bottom of server
The listening fd remains open for further accept() calls.
Production code must handle errors, EOF and partial I/O.
end note
@enduml
